  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "From the academy window a nearby bamboo grove shows Qing Mao Mountain’s spear bamboo: each stick straight as a line, the ends sharp like spear tips.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Around Gu Yue Village the same growth is a bamboo forest where grass is luxuriant, white flowers endless, and green spear bamboo stands straight like pencils, the forest resembling a clump of jade rods. Under thick cloud the grove is deadly silent, each green spear bamboo a straight up-and-down line. When moonlight returns, the forest is like a conscious pond: green jade colors of spear bamboo flash, snowy frost flowers fill the ground, and Dragonpill crickets flash crimson on green grass and wild flowers under the bamboo.",
      "chapters": [
        13
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deeper in, the ground is a green carpet of grass with blossoming wild flowers, mossy stones, and yellow bamboo shoots; green spear bamboo stalks flash past under gentle moonlight.",
      "chapters": [
        14
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "From the academy window on Qing Mao Mountain, a bamboo grove sits nearby. The stalks are Qing Mao Mountain’s spear bamboo: straight as a line, with ends sharp like spear tips.",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "spear-bamboo-around-the-village",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Around Gu Yue Village, the same growth is called a bamboo forest. Grass and white flowers fill the ground between green spear bamboo that stands like a clump of jade rods.",
      "chapters": [
        13
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "spear-bamboo-around-the-village",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_gu_yue_village"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan walks that forest at night while hunting clues to the Flower Wine Monk treasure, pouring green bamboo wine onto stone and grass to draw a Liquor worm. When moonlight breaks through cloud, Dragonpill crickets flash red among the grass and wild flowers under the bamboo.",
      "chapters": [
        13
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "night-search-for-the-liquor-worm",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_flower_wine_monk",
        "gu_liquor_worm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Liquor worm later glues itself to a spear bamboo pole there, drinks the wine, and flies deeper into the forest before leading him out toward a mountain crevice.",
      "chapters": [
        14
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "night-search-for-the-liquor-worm",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
